# Copy to .runtime/vibe/.env on the server, or set these in host environment settings.
# No credentials belong in this example or in GitHub.
# Choose ONE model connection.

# Option A: use the project's separate interactive ChatGPT/Codex login.
# Model availability depends on your account. This name is from the inspected upstream provider list.
LANGCHAIN_PROVIDER=openai-codex
LANGCHAIN_MODEL_NAME=openai-codex/gpt-6-sol
# Then run npm run vibe:login in a terminal on this same host.

# Option B: Ollama (local, no API key). Change to a model actually installed on your server.
# LANGCHAIN_PROVIDER=ollama
# LANGCHAIN_MODEL_NAME=your-installed-model
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434

# Option C: an API-key provider. Set the key securely outside source control.
# LANGCHAIN_PROVIDER=openai
# LANGCHAIN_MODEL_NAME=your-provider-model
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# For remote AI requests, set API_AUTH_KEY to a private app-access key on the server.
# Enter that app key (not a provider key) in ChartScope > Connection setup.
# API_AUTH_KEY=
